{
  "name": "mosquito",
  "_about": "A mosquito -- the common house mosquito (Culex pipiens), a female 6 mm long: slender and long-legged; a small round head with dark wrap-round eyes, the long proboscis held forward and down with short palps beside it; antennae with short whorls of hair; a humped, scaly brown thorax; a long thin abdomen, brown ringed pale at the front of each segment; very long thin legs, the hind pair held up behind; narrow scaled wings laid flat over the abdomen. Variant: the male (great bushy plumed antennae, long palps, no bite). Coat: the tiger mosquito (Aedes albopictus: black, banded white, a white line down the thorax). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/flies.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait; the wings at rest laid back over the abdomen, swung out and beating in the variant \"flying\").",
